    "['admin-vrrp vrid [parameter1] ignore-if-down', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'vrrp 10 track shutdown', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nvrrp 10 track shutdown\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `admin-vrrp vrid 10 ignore-if-down` command makes the VRRP group continue operating even if the interface goes down.\\n- The Cisco equivalent is `vrrp <group> track shutdown`, which similarly prevents VRRP from shutting down when the interface state changes.\\n- Both commands serve the same purpose of maintaining VRRP operation despite interface state changes.', 'trans_template': 'vrrp 10 track shutdown'}]]": 1,
