    "['service-location [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'redundancy', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'redundancy', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For Cisco devices, the equivalent concept to Huawei\\'s `service-location` would typically involve redundancy protocols like HSRP or GLBP, but there isn\\'t a direct 1:1 command translation. The closest Cisco equivalent would be configuring a redundancy group with tracking, but the exact implementation depends on the service context.\\n\\nSince `service-location` in Huawei is used for service redundancy and tracking (paired with VRRP in this case), the Cisco equivalent would involve configuring a redundancy protocol (like HSRP) with tracking, but without the exact service-location abstraction.\\n\\nThe closest Cisco-style configuration would be:\\n##\\nredundancy\\n protocol hsrp\\n track 21 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/3\\n##\\n\\n(Note: This is an approximation since Cisco doesn\\'t have a direct \"service-location\" concept. The actual implementation would require a more context-specific approach depending on the service being configured.)', 'trans_template': 'redundancy'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'protocol hsrp', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'protocol hsrp', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For Cisco devices, the equivalent concept to Huawei\\'s `service-location` would typically involve redundancy protocols like HSRP or GLBP, but there isn\\'t a direct 1:1 command translation. The closest Cisco equivalent would be configuring a redundancy group with tracking, but the exact implementation depends on the service context.\\n\\nSince `service-location` in Huawei is used for service redundancy and tracking (paired with VRRP in this case), the Cisco equivalent would involve configuring a redundancy protocol (like HSRP) with tracking, but without the exact service-location abstraction.\\n\\nThe closest Cisco-style configuration would be:\\n##\\nredundancy\\n protocol hsrp\\n track 21 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/3\\n##\\n\\n(Note: This is an approximation since Cisco doesn\\'t have a direct \"service-location\" concept. The actual implementation would require a more context-specific approach depending on the service being configured.)', 'trans_template': 'protocol hsrp'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'track 21 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/3', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'track 21 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For Cisco devices, the equivalent concept to Huawei\\'s `service-location` would typically involve redundancy protocols like HSRP or GLBP, but there isn\\'t a direct 1:1 command translation. The closest Cisco equivalent would be configuring a redundancy group with tracking, but the exact implementation depends on the service context.\\n\\nSince `service-location` in Huawei is used for service redundancy and tracking (paired with VRRP in this case), the Cisco equivalent would involve configuring a redundancy protocol (like HSRP) with tracking, but without the exact service-location abstraction.\\n\\nThe closest Cisco-style configuration would be:\\n##\\nredundancy\\n protocol hsrp\\n track 21 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/3\\n##\\n\\n(Note: This is an approximation since Cisco doesn\\'t have a direct \"service-location\" concept. The actual implementation would require a more context-specific approach depending on the service being configured.)', 'trans_template': 'track 21 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/3'}]]": 1,
    "['location slot [parameter1] engine [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'service location 21 rack 1 chassis 0', 'parent_command': ['redundancy'], 'root': 'redundancy', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the HUAWEI `location slot 1 engine 0` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nservice location 21 rack 1 chassis 0\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, the equivalent concept for specifying service location typically uses \"rack chassis slot\" terminology (for physical devices) or \"node\" terminology (for virtual contexts). However, exact equivalents may vary depending on Cisco platform (ASR, CSR, etc.). The above translation assumes a Cisco ASR platform where:\\n- \"slot 1\" becomes \"rack 1\"\\n- \"engine 0\" becomes \"chassis 0\"', 'trans_template': 'service location 21 rack 1 chassis 0'}]]": 1,
