    "['remote-ipv6 [parameter1] prefix-length [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 route 2001:db8:1::/41 <next-hop-ipv6-or-interface>', 'parent_command': ['cgn instance dslite1 id 21'], 'root': 'cgn instance dslite1 id 21', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nipv6 route 2001:db8:1::/41 <next-hop-ipv6-or-interface>\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, the `remote-ipv6` command from Huawei (which specifies the DS-Lite remote IPv6 prefix) would typically be implemented as an IPv6 static route pointing to the AFTR (Address Family Transition Router) or the next-hop interface. The exact next-hop or interface would need to be specified in the Cisco command (replace `<next-hop-ipv6-or-interface>` with the appropriate value). Huawei's `remote-ipv6` defines the IPv6 prefix for DS-Lite tunnel endpoints, while Cisco achieves this through routing.\", 'trans_template': 'ipv6 route 2001:db8:1::/41 <next-hop-ipv6-or-interface>'}]]": 1,
